        <mxCell id="AeTiZLamMoqDxRa9LT03-68" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" value="&lt;b&gt;Sharding / Partitioning&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;by &lt;b&gt;Range&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;to accomodate a lot of data in less expensive servers:" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="498.25" x="69.86999999999999" y="590" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AeTiZLamMoqDxRa9LT03-74" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" value="- RDBMS: Relational Database Management System&lt;div&gt;- RDB: Relational Database&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Standardd relational databases run on single computer / server&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Example of Relational Databases: MySQL, Oracle Database, Postgres Database&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Data in RDB&#39;s are stored in one or more t&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;ables. Each tables contain r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;ecords. It also stores relationships among recrods of one table to the records of another table.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); font-family: monospace; font-size: 0px; white-space: nowrap;&quot;&gt;%3CmxGraphModel%3E%3Croot%3E%3CmxCell%20id%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3CmxCell%20id%3D%221%22%20parent%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3CmxCell%20id%3D%222%22%20value%3D%22RDB%22%20style%3D%22text%3Bhtml%3D1%3Balign%3Dcenter%3BverticalAlign%3Dmiddle%3BwhiteSpace%3Dwrap%3Brounded%3D0%3B%22%20vertex%3D%221%22%20parent%3D%221%22%3E%3CmxGeometry%20x%3D%2270%22%20y%3D%22130%22%20width%3D%2260%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20as%3D%22geometry%22%2F%3E%3C%2FmxCell%3E%3C%2Froot%3E%3C%2FmxGraphModel%3E&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="481.5" x="236.68" y="-1025" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AeTiZLamMoqDxRa9LT03-76" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" value="Server" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="60" x="83.31" y="-140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AeTiZLamMoqDxRa9LT03-78" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height: 140%;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;Why is there a limitation in different databases in very large scale?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;- these DBs are run and built for a single computer/server system (in contrast to a distributed system)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;- there&#39;s physical limitation in building the highest performing single server system&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; - Compute (CPU)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; - Storage (DISC)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; - Memory (RAM)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="125" width="541.5" x="233.56" y="-230" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AeTiZLamMoqDxRa9LT03-80" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" value="&lt;b&gt;Examples of Relational Data:&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="172.25" x="73.56" y="-640" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AeTiZLamMoqDxRa9LT03-81" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="For example, if Facebook stored their social media data in a RDB, they may store user&#39;s personal information in a table called users, all user posts in a table called posts, and store all comments in another table. &#xa;&#xa;&#xa;Similar type of data is stored in a single table to aid in querying, grouping and analyzing. A facebook user will have a single record on the users table. If the user created posts, their corresponding post records will be in the posts table. The same table will contain post records of other users. These records will have information about the corresponding user id to signify the relationship among the user and their posts." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="573.75" x="236.68" y="-860" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AeTiZLamMoqDxRa9LT03-84" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/jpeg,;clipPath=inset(15.09% 7.67% 0% 8% round 20%);" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="272.6556719367589" width="480.71" x="233.55999999999997" y="-590" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AeTiZLamMoqDxRa9LT03-89" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div&gt;Big Data System (overly&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;simplified)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="202.63" x="328.98" y="1920" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
